# KASTR image context (0.13.1): the built Linux binary, its version marker,
# the other platforms' feed binaries and the entrypoint -- nothing else. The
# repo holds ~1 GB of browser zips and archives that must never reach the
# daemon. Later rules win; a `!` re-includes below the `*`.
*
!dist/linux/KASTR
!dist/linux/BUILT_VERSION
!dist/updates
!docker

# The container serves its own Linux binary from sys.executable, so the
# linux feed copy is redundant; the Chrome for Testing zips (~200 MB each,
# /api/update/browser) are left out to keep the image small -- delete the
# next line to ship them when the container is the hub for desktop clients
# that need a browser update.
dist/updates/browser
dist/updates/linux
